# Per-run ignore for the agentic-runs repo.
# A run's output is committed; the agentic runtime's *scratch*
# state is not. The committed-run vs. live-run distinction is
# enforced by the substrate (the agentic transport only writes
# to runs/<run_id>/ *after* the run has been finalized; live
# scratch is held in ~/agentic/runs/<run_id>/, the working
# directory, not in this repo).

# Generated by the index-card writer on a live run before the
# run is committed. After the run reaches EXPLAINED/FAILED,
# the commit phase copies the final report.html / index_card.html
# into output/ and these ignore rules no longer apply.
**/output/*.tmp
**/output/*.part

# Lockfile directory. The locks/ directory itself is committed
# (it's the convention: the lockfile history is part of the
# audit trail). The actual .lock files are committed-or-cleaned
# at run end per the README; we do NOT ignore them by default
# because the trail of lock-acquisition is forensic data.
# Uncomment the next line to ignore lockfiles (NOT recommended
# for the default run history):
# *.lock

# Backup copies the transport may stage before atomic rename.
*.bak
*.tmp

# Local override files (per-developer config; not committed)
.env
.env.local
